<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="SRFR-021" project="set-regarding-and-field-mapping-resolver-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Extract PolymorphicPicker Fluent v9 shared component</title>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <estimated-effort>6h</estimated-effort>
    <actual-effort></actual-effort>
    <assigned>AI Agent</assigned>
    <started></started>
    <completed></completed>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-group>A</parallel-group>
    <tags>shared-lib,fluent-v9,component,wave-2,spaarke-ui-components</tags>
    <depends-on></depends-on>
    <wave>2</wave>
  </metadata>

  <prompt><![CDATA[
Both RegardingResolver and AssociationResolver privately implement the same picker:
a dropdown-plus-toolbar-icon that opens the OOB `Xrm.Utility.lookupObjects` dialog
for a chosen entity type. This duplication is a candidate extraction target for the
shared component library per FR-C2-01 + FR-A1-03.

Extract this to a single Fluent v9 component `PolymorphicPicker` in
`@spaarke/ui-components`. Both PCFs will consume it after Wave 3 (RegardingResolver)
and Wave 5 (AssociationResolver) refactors. The component must render in Fluent v9
only (no v8 imports), theme via semantic tokens (dark-mode safe), and expose a clean
props contract that does NOT couple to `ComponentFramework` types.
  ]]></prompt>

  <role>Fluent UI v9 React component author familiar with the Spaarke shared component library conventions, the `fluent-v9-component-authoring` pattern, and Xrm.Utility.lookupObjects contracts.</role>

  <goal><![CDATA[
`PolymorphicPicker` component ships in `@spaarke/ui-components` with a documented
props contract, Fluent v9 semantic-token theming, storybook/harness entry rendering
the component with a sample catalog, and unit tests covering menu open, catalog
rendering, onSelect callback, and disabled/readOnly states. Both RegardingResolver
and AssociationResolver can adopt this component with a single import in later
waves.
  ]]></goal>

  <inputs>
    <file purpose="spec">projects/set-regarding-and-field-mapping-resolver-r1/spec.md</file>
    <file purpose="plan">projects/set-regarding-and-field-mapping-resolver-r1/plan.md</file>
    <file purpose="project-claude">projects/set-regarding-and-field-mapping-resolver-r1/CLAUDE.md</file>
    <file purpose="pattern">.claude/patterns/ui/fluent-v9-component-authoring.md</file>
    <file purpose="pattern">.claude/patterns/ui/fluent-v9-theming.md</file>
    <file purpose="pattern">.claude/patterns/pcf/fluent-v9-modern-theming.md</file>
    <file purpose="skill">.claude/skills/fluent-v9-component/SKILL.md</file>
    <file purpose="adr">.claude/adr/ADR-012-shared-component-library.md</file>
    <file purpose="adr">.claude/adr/ADR-022-pcf-platform-libraries.md</file>
    <file purpose="reference">src/client/pcf/RegardingResolver/</file>
    <file purpose="reference">src/client/pcf/AssociationResolver/</file>
  </inputs>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-012">Shared lib API boundary — component MUST NOT import `ComponentFramework` types; accept `webApi`/host bridge as prop or via typed shim</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-022">No bundling of React or Fluent v9 — peerDependencies pattern for the package</constraint>
    <constraint source="convention">Fluent v9 exclusively; NO imports from `@fluentui/react` v8</constraint>
    <constraint source="convention">Semantic tokens only; NO hardcoded color literals (dark-mode safe)</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Public export via `src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/index.ts` — both component and its props type</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Component must render in both PCF-hosted and standalone-story contexts</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Tests use React Testing Library idioms; no `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;` (TS equivalent — inject stub callbacks, not fetch mocks)</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">TypeScript strict mode. No `any`. Prefer explicit prop types.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>ui/fluent-v9-component</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/patterns/ui/fluent-v9-component-authoring.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/ui/fluent-v9-theming.md</file>
      <file>.claude/skills/fluent-v9-component/SKILL.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-012-shared-component-library.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Fluent v9 Menu-driven picker" location=".claude/patterns/ui/fluent-v9-component-authoring.md">
        Use `Menu`, `MenuTrigger`, `MenuPopover`, `MenuList`, `MenuItem` for the entity list;
        the trigger is a `ToolbarButton` with `SearchRegular` icon. On item click, invoke
        `Xrm.Utility.lookupObjects({ entityTypes: [entityType], allowMultiSelect: false })`
        and pipe the promise result to `onSelect`.
      </pattern>
      <pattern name="Semantic-token theming" location=".claude/patterns/ui/fluent-v9-theming.md">
        Use `tokens.colorNeutralForeground1` / `tokens.colorNeutralBackground1` and never
        raw hex or named CSS colors. Verify by rendering in `webDarkTheme`.
      </pattern>
      <pattern name="Shared-lib peerDependencies" location=".claude/adr/ADR-022-pcf-platform-libraries.md">
        React + Fluent v9 are peerDependencies; the shared lib must not re-bundle them,
        or PCF bundles will double-include and break at runtime.
      </pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <context>
    <background>
      RegardingResolver and AssociationResolver each ship a near-identical picker: a small
      row with a title and a search-icon toolbar button that opens a Fluent v9 menu of
      supported entity types, then delegates to `Xrm.Utility.lookupObjects` for the actual
      record picking. Consolidating into `PolymorphicPicker` in the shared lib eliminates
      the duplication and gives future PCFs a canonical picker component. This ships in
      the same `@spaarke/ui-components` minor release as tasks 020, 022, 023 per A-05.
    </background>
    <dependencies></dependencies>
    <related-work>
      <item>Wave 3 task SRFR-030+ adopts PolymorphicPicker in RegardingResolver.</item>
      <item>Wave 5 task SRFR-050+ adopts PolymorphicPicker in AssociationResolver.</item>
    </related-work>
  </context>

  <steps>
    <step order="0" name="Context Check">Verify context &lt; 60%. Read spec.md FR-A1-03, FR-C2-01. Read the fluent-v9 pattern + skill docs.</step>
    <step order="1" name="Study Current Implementations">Read the picker implementations in RegardingResolver and AssociationResolver. Identify the common contract and any divergent details. Record in notes/task-021-picker-diff.md.</step>
    <step order="2" name="Design Props Contract">Draft `PolymorphicPickerProps` interface: `catalog`, `onSelect`, optional `disabled`, `readOnly`, `title` (default "Related Record"). Confirm no `ComponentFramework` type leakage.</step>
    <step order="3" name="Scaffold Component">Create `src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/PolymorphicPicker/PolymorphicPicker.tsx`. Implement title + `ToolbarButton` + Fluent v9 `Menu` driven by `catalog`.</step>
    <step order="4" name="Wire lookupObjects">On MenuItem click, call `Xrm.Utility.lookupObjects({ entityTypes: [entityType], allowMultiSelect: false })`; invoke `onSelect(entityType, recordId, recordName)` on the first result. Handle empty/cancel gracefully.</step>
    <step order="5" name="Semantic Tokens">Apply `makeStyles` + `tokens.*` for all colors and spacing. Verify by rendering in `webLightTheme` and `webDarkTheme`.</step>
    <step order="6" name="Public Export">Add `export { PolymorphicPicker, PolymorphicPickerProps } from './components/PolymorphicPicker/PolymorphicPicker';` (or component-level index.ts) to `src/index.ts`.</step>
    <step order="7" name="Storybook / Harness Entry">If repo has storybook or a component harness (verify via Glob), add a story rendering PolymorphicPicker with a sample catalog. If not, add a minimal `PolymorphicPicker.stories.tsx` or documented usage snippet in the component README.</step>
    <step order="8" name="Unit Tests">Add tests: (a) menu opens on toolbar-button click; (b) MenuList renders one MenuItem per catalog entry; (c) selecting an item invokes onSelect with expected (entityType, recordId, recordName); (d) disabled/readOnly props suppress interaction. Mock `Xrm.Utility.lookupObjects` via a global test double.</step>
    <step order="9" name="Build + Test">Run `npm run build` and `npm test` in `Spaarke.UI.Components/`. Fix TS strict errors.</step>
    <step order="10" name="Step 9.5 Quality Gate">Invoke `/fluent-v9-component`, `/code-review`, and `/adr-check` on the new component. Address findings.</step>
    <step order="11" name="Update Task Status">Update TASK-INDEX.md 🔲 → ✅ for SRFR-021. Reset current-task.md for next task.</step>
  </steps>

  <tools>
    <tool name="Read">Load pattern docs + existing picker implementations</tool>
    <tool name="Write">Create PolymorphicPicker.tsx and tests</tool>
    <tool name="Edit">Update src/index.ts exports</tool>
    <tool name="Glob">Locate existing storybook / harness entries if present</tool>
    <tool name="Grep">Confirm no `@fluentui/react` v8 imports leak in</tool>
    <tool name="Bash">Run `npm run build` and `npm test` in shared lib package</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/PolymorphicPicker/PolymorphicPicker.tsx</output>
    <output type="code" conditional="if-index-file-exists">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/PolymorphicPicker/index.ts</output>
    <output type="test">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/PolymorphicPicker/__tests__/PolymorphicPicker.test.tsx</output>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/index.ts</output>
    <output type="story-or-doc">Storybook story or usage snippet in component README</output>
    <output type="notes">projects/set-regarding-and-field-mapping-resolver-r1/notes/task-021-picker-diff.md</output>
    <output type="docs">projects/set-regarding-and-field-mapping-resolver-r1/tasks/TASK-INDEX.md (🔲 → ✅ for SRFR-021)</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Component builds under strict TypeScript with zero errors and zero `any` usages.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No imports from `@fluentui/react` v8 anywhere in the new component (verified via Grep).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Storybook story or harness entry renders the component with a sample catalog.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Unit tests cover: menu opens on icon click; entity list matches catalog; onSelect fires with expected (entityType, recordId, recordName); disabled and readOnly suppress interaction.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Component exported from `@spaarke/ui-components` public surface (`src/index.ts`), both component and props type.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Dark-mode check passes: no hardcoded color literals; semantic tokens only.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Component contract accepts no `ComponentFramework` types (verified by reviewing prop types).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`/fluent-v9-component`, `/code-review`, and `/adr-check` pass at Step 9.5.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
</task>
